  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The side length $x$ of a cube increases at a constant rate of 3 units per second. Find the rate of change of the following when $x=2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Surface area.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$72\\text{ units}^2/\\text{s}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}S&=6x^2\\\\\\frac{dS}{dx}&=12x\\\\\\frac{dS}{dt}&=\\frac{dS}{dx}\\frac{dx}{dt}\\\\\\frac{dS}{dt}&=12x(3)\\\\\\frac{dS}{dt}&=36x\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $x=2$, $\\dfrac{dS}{dt}=36(2)=72\\text{ units}^2/\\text{s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Volume.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$36\\text{ units}^3/\\text{s}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V&=x^3\\\\\\frac{dV}{dx}&=3x^2\\\\\\frac{dV}{dt}&=\\frac{dV}{dx}\\frac{dx}{dt}\\\\\\frac{dV}{dt}&=3x^2(3)\\\\\\frac{dV}{dt}&=9x^2\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $x=2$, $\\dfrac{dV}{dt}=9(2)^2=36\\text{ units}^3/\\text{s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      }
    ]
  },
